EXTENSION "ARMDef_Faith_and_Flame_Narbonnais_DucaruOfTytalus" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Faith & Flame - Ducaru of Tytalus"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Faith_and_Flame_Core_Ext"

    # Ducaru of Tytalus (Chapter Seven: Narbonnais, p109): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t74dec5d31f4897d546cdf8 ^"Ducaru of Tytalus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t89e3531582ad22c2eae1be ^"Stella Durus"]
            ^"Age" STRING "44 (Apparent age: 34)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Boastful +2, Calculating +2, Reckless +2"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 109
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A Romanian arrival apprenticed in the Theban Tribunal, Ducaru joined the covenant with a very individual goal. He intends to infiltrate the nobility to broker marriages and alliances and has begun doing so, creating a Norman persona. He listens more than he speaks, influencing active participants, rather than participating himself. Ducaru prefers making suggestions and observing the effects versus acting directly. He plays a dangerous game, one which could have him facing charges at Tribunal should it become well-known. Jean Marie suspects it, as the Tytalus occasionally pumps him for information about the local nobility through the Jerbiton’s troubadour contacts.\n\nNever seen without his distinctive goatskin cap, Ducaru’s mastery of Mentem magics makes his goal a possibility, but his expert knowledge of Vim only seems to draw suspicion. He does not consider himself evil, but he also does not allow morals or society’s expectations to limit his actions. He often takes actions, especially unexpected actions, simply to observe the outcome. The least involved in covenant operations, Ducaru always contributes at the most opportune moment. He keeps a game of chess running in a Perpignan tavern, where he is in the process of beating Etienne of Ara Maxima Nova. The two have been trading games for months. Redcaps now frequent the tavern, keeping current on the state of the game and placing wagers on who will win."
    }

}
